From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <106575910+KRRT7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:26:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Live: keep torch out of the UI process

Only the voice worker runs torch, but the UI process loaded it too, plus a
second CUDA runtime next to ONNX Runtime's once face swap started. Idle UI
process: 649 -> 336 MB RAM, 1.86 -> 1.02 GB committed. During face swap:
-370 MB RAM, -860 MB committed. Same fps.

- Paste-back blends with cv2 instead of torch CUDA (swap and GFPGAN).
  The torch path paid an upload and a download per face and was slower
  at face-crop sizes (RTX 4060: 0.68 vs 0.15 ms at 250 px, 1.24 vs
  0.43 ms at 400 px); output is identical within 1 level.
- The fp16 inswapper / CUDA-graph choice asks the configured ONNX
  Runtime providers instead of torch.cuda. platform_info drops its
  unused HAS_TORCH_CUDA, which imported torch.
- _vendor.modules preloads the CUDA/cuDNN DLLs with
  onnxruntime.preload_dlls() (torch's bundled copies, found without
  importing torch), and stops albumentations (via insightface) from
  importing torch. It also disables albumentations' PyPI update check,
  a network request on every import.
- AUDIO_SAMPLE_RATE moves to rvc.realtime.constants, so the settings,
  audio and Live modules no longer import rvc.realtime.core (torch,
  faiss, scipy, transformers). The worker imports VoiceChanger only in
  the child process.
- The Voice tab reads speakers_id with a restricted unpickler
  (rvc.lib.checkpoint_meta) instead of torch.load: no torch and no
  weights loaded, and only containers and tensor-rebuild stubs resolve.
- app.py imports rvc.lib.zluda only in client mode, the one mode that
  runs voice in this process; the worker imports it itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Applio-Commit: c20029b680bec5933024f70a80075ac2778a31c8 (as merged in 9ead3828)
